  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-3" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.3</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Ranged Foundation &amp; Fire Cape</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Use the Final Dawn lamp for a small quest bridge, build a reproducible crossbow-and-bolt kit, split the Ranged training with two light quests, then earn a Fire Cape by ranging Jad.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Final Dawn lamp → actual 62 Ranged → Troll Romance → The Curse of Arrav → deterministic weapon and ammo → Ranged 70 → two-quest break → Ranged 75 → ranged Fight Caves → Fire Cape."
        stats={["62 Ranged is Arrav's quest gate, not the Fight Caves target", "75 Ranged is the normal first-Jad readiness target, not a game requirement", "No Bowfa, blowpipe, rune-crossbow drop or Rigour dependency"]}
        unlocks={["The Curse of Arrav and Zemouregal's Fort", "A Ruff Situation and Crab Quest", "Fire Cape and a remaining enchanted-bolt reserve"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>3.2 handoff:</strong> the mandatory route has actual 60+ Ranged <em>before</em> the one Final Dawn lamp; 70 Prayer/Defence, Piety, Barrows gloves, Ava's accumulator, 70+ Smithing and at least 61 Fletching after Devious Minds and Final Dawn. Read your live levels and bank. No rune crossbow, black mask, Slayer helmet, Moon/Eclipse armour, Bowfa/crystal, blowpipe, Rigour or Ava's assembler is guaranteed. Exiles' Slayer/Crafting/Runecraft XP is real, but none is a gate on this page.</div>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Do not merge the two Ranged targets.</strong> Actual <strong>62 Ranged is only The Curse of Arrav's hard quest gate</strong>. It is <strong>not</strong> the recommended Fight Caves level. The default route continues to <strong>actual 75 Ranged before its first Jad attempt</strong>; experienced players can try around 70, and training toward 80 after a difficult attempt is a bounded comfort adjustment, not a reason to farm rare gear.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quest bridge · spend the lamp once</div><h2>Close Arrav's one missing gate, then do the quests.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i33-ranged-62" number="1" title="Bridge to actual 62 Ranged after the Final Dawn lamp">
        <p>Chapter 3.2 allocates its <strong>single 55,000-XP combat lamp to Ranged by default</strong>. If optional play already left Ranged comfortably around Fire-Cape readiness, that same lamp goes to <strong>Magic</strong> for a later actual-75 quest gate instead. Do not count the lamp in both skills. After it is used, inspect live Ranged XP. At an exact level-60 floor, <strong>273,742 + 55,000 = 328,742 XP</strong>, while level 62 starts at <strong>333,804 XP</strong>: only <strong>5,062 XP</strong> remains in that conservative case. If the lamp went to Magic, simply train the actual live Ranged gap instead.</p>
        <p>For this small bridge, buy a <strong>Dorgeshuun crossbow and bone bolts or bone-bolt packs</strong> from <strong>Nardok's Bone Weapons in the Dorgesh-Kaan mine</strong>. The Lost Tribe, completed in Chapter 2, opened this goblin area; Nardok stocks both the weapon and its cheap ammunition. Bone bolts work with Ava's accumulator. Range a low-defence target such as the <strong>Gemstone Crab</strong> in Varlamore's Tlati Rainforest (follow the caves between its moving nests), Ammonite crabs on Fossil Island, or another convenient crab. Ordinary Ranged-friendly Slayer tasks are a change of scene. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dorgeshuun_crossbow" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Weapon and shop</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Gemstone_Crab" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Gemstone Crab access</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Stop immediately at actual 62 Ranged.</strong> Handle Troll Romance and The Curse of Arrav before the longer 62→70 training block.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-troll-romance" number="2" title="Complete Troll Romance">
        <p>Speak to <strong>Ug in the south-west room on the middle level of Troll Stronghold</strong>. Troll Stronghold/Death Plateau are already complete. Reach the stronghold via Trollheim Teleport if available, or take climbing boots for the mountain approach; fairy ring <strong>AJR</strong> and the secret door near the Fremennik Slayer Dungeon are another route. Bring <strong>one iron bar, one maple or yew log, rope</strong>, and wax materials: <strong>bucket of wax, cake tin and swamp tar</strong>. To make a bucket of wax if absent, use insect repellent on a beehive, then an empty bucket; combine the materials for the sled as the quest directs. Check the bank before gathering again. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Troll_Romance/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current preparation and route</a>.</p>
        <p>The quest visits Burthorpe, Trollweiss Mountain and the stronghold again; pack travel, food, Prayer restores and ordinary combat gear, but bank between phases. For the <strong>Arrg</strong> fight, be ready <em>before</em> starting the dialogue: he attacks with melee and Ranged and can hit hard. Use your existing defensive gear, protection prayer and food, keep health high, and teleport rather than risking an empty-supply finish. This quest fight is not a safe death. Claim <strong>8,000 Agility and 4,000 Strength XP</strong>. Troll Romance is the direct prerequisite for Arrav.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-arrav" number="3" title="Complete The Curse of Arrav; leave the zombie drops optional">
        <p><strong>Hard gate audit:</strong> actual <strong>64 Mining, 62 Ranged, 62 Thieving, 61 Agility, 58 Strength and 37 Slayer</strong>, plus <strong>Defender of Varrock and Troll Romance</strong>. The earlier route covers every gate once Step 1 reaches actual 62 Ranged. Begin with <strong>Elias White at the Uzer Oasis</strong>, reachable from fairy ring <strong>DLQ</strong>. This is the Old School version of the quest; do not use an original RuneScape 3 item list. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Curse_of_Arrav/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current OSRS item and phase guide</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Stage the real items by phase:</strong> three dwellberries and a <strong>ring of life</strong> (consumed by the tomb jar); any pickaxe for the Trollweiss rubble; then <strong>any crossbow, a mith grapple and insulated boots</strong> for the base's fire traps and electric sewer. A Dorgeshuun crossbow works for the grapple phase. Check the bank first. If missing, make a ring of life by enchanting a diamond ring with level-57 Lvl-4 Enchant; buy insulated boots from a Slayer equipment shop. A deterministic mith grapple uses a <strong>mith grapple tip</strong> smithed from a mithril bar at 59 Smithing, attached to a mithril bolt and finished with rope at 59 Fletching—both levels are already cleared. Bring food, Prayer restores, emergency teleport, a low-weight travel setup and spare inventory slots. Bank/regear between the Uzer tomb, Trollweiss and Digsite base instead of carrying everything at once.</p>
        <p><strong>Combat and traversal:</strong> move away when the tomb's golem begins its multi-hit ground attack; Protect from Melee while passing ice trolls; mine the blocked Trollweiss tunnels; wear insulated boots in the sewer and grapple over the fire traps. For the final <strong>Arrav</strong> fight, Protect from Melee for ordinary hits, move to his side/behind his directional axe swing, and stay out of the venom trails left by small zombie adds. A banked Ranged or Magic weapon can clear those adds; the later Fight Cave crossbow is not a prerequisite for this quest. Claim <strong>40,000 XP each in Mining, Thieving and Agility</strong> and <strong>Zemouregal's Fort access</strong>. Do <strong>not</strong> farm Armoured Zombies: a zombie axe or helmet drop is optional, never a route gate.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Deterministic Ranged kit · one outcome</div><h2>Audit the bank before training any production skill.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i33-ranged-kit" number="4" title="Secure sufficient deterministic Fight Cave ammo and the ranged weapon floor">
        <p><strong>Bank audit first:</strong> count plain adamant bolts, ruby bolts (e), diamond bolts (e), adamant bars, cut/uncut rubies and diamonds, and any existing rune crossbow. Count usable ammunition rather than demanding an arbitrary Smithing or Fletching level. The planning stock is about <strong>1,200 plain adamant bolts</strong> for ordinary Fight Cave waves and retry headroom, <strong>250 diamond bolts (e)</strong> for Jad/high-defence targets and later quests, and a <strong>bounded 300 ruby bolts (e)</strong> reserved mainly for later high-HP bosses such as Galvek and quest Vorkath. These are working buffers, <em>not</em> exact consumption predictions; top up against real attempts and remaining stock. Diamond (e), not ruby (e), is the natural Jad accuracy switch here. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/TzHaar_Fight_Cave/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Fight Cave supply guidance</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Enchantment_spells" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Bolt effects</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Weapon floor:</strong> if an RCB is already banked, use it. Otherwise buy <strong>adamantite limbs from the Keldagrim crossbow stall</strong>; knife a mahogany log into a <strong>mahogany stock</strong>, attach the limbs with a hammer, and add a <strong>crossbow string</strong> at <strong>61 Fletching</strong> for an adamant crossbow. Check for a string first; if missing, cook raw beef into <strong>sinew</strong> and spin it at a wheel at 10 Crafting, or spin banked tree roots. The route guarantees 61+ Fletching already. No runite-limb or RCB drop is required. The adamant crossbow's <strong>+78 Ranged accuracy</strong> versus an RCB's <strong>+90</strong> was only about <strong>4–4.6% behind in our pinned DPS comparisons</strong> for Jad, Galvek, quest Vorkath and quest Leviathan. That modest tradeoff buys a deterministic setup. <strong>Broad bolts require an RCB or better</strong>, so they do not solve the adamant-crossbow path. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Adamant_crossbow" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Crossbow assembly</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crossbow_(weapon)" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Weapon/ammo table</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Only if the bank is short: make the remaining bolts" label="Conditional production">
          <p><strong>73 Smithing and 63–65 Fletching are conditional production branches, not universal Chapter 3.3 requirements.</strong> The Quest Cape itself later forces only 72 Smithing; 73 exists here solely to smith adamant bolt bases if you lack enough bolts. Train only the live gap with banked ore/bars or a normal Smithing method, then smith one adamant bar into <strong>10 unfinished bolts</strong> at an anvil and feather them at 61 Fletching. For a complete zero-stock example, 1,200 plain + 250 diamond + 300 ruby = <strong>1,750 bolts from 175 bars and 1,750 feathers</strong>; subtract every usable bolt already banked before mining/smelting. The route's 70+ Mining can provide adamantite ore, and the Blast Furnace can smelt ore with coal if bars are short. This is a finite stock, not an unbounded ammo grind.</p>
          <p>If tipped stock is short, train to <strong>actual 63 Fletching for ruby</strong> and <strong>actual 65 for diamond</strong> only as needed; use banked logs/bows or other ordinary Fletching materials for the live gap. Chisel a cut ruby or diamond into <strong>12 tips</strong>, attach tips to finished adamant bolts in groups of 10, then use <strong>Enchant Crossbow Bolt</strong> on the standard spellbook: ruby needs 49 Magic, diamond 57 Magic, both already covered. In the zero-stock example, roughly <strong>25 rubies</strong> and <strong>21 diamonds</strong> yield enough tips for 300/250 finished bolts. Check banked enchanted bolts and tips before cutting gems. Do not spend these enchanted bolts on low-defence crab training. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Adamant_bolts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Bolt production</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ruby_bolt_tips" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ruby tips</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Diamond_bolt_tips" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Diamond tips</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Tick this one outcome when the crossbow and usable stock are ready.</strong> There are no separate required progress boxes for RCB, Bowfa, 73 Smithing or 65 Fletching; an existing bank can bypass production entirely.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Ranged · first long interval</div><h2>Train in two pieces, with quests between them.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i33-ranged-70" number="5" title="Train actual 62 → 70 Ranged with cheap ammunition">
        <p>Return to the <strong>Dorgeshuun crossbow + bone-bolt</strong> setup at the Gemstone Crab, Ammonite crabs or another low-defence crab. Gemstone Crab is a low-damage, nearly limitless target but moves between Tlati Rainforest nests about every ten minutes; the cave network takes you to its current location. Ammonite crabs offer an ordinary Fossil Island alternative. Ranged-friendly Slayer assignments can break the routine. Keep the hard-won plain and enchanted adamant bolts for the Fight Caves and later bosses. Read live XP and stop at <strong>actual 70 Ranged</strong>.</p>
        <p>A practiced player <em>may</em> try the Fight Caves around 70, but that is an early-attempt option, not the default handoff. The normal route takes a short quest break and then finishes 75 before Jad.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-ruff" number="6" title="Quest break: complete A Ruff Situation">
        <p>This short quest, released <strong>8 September 2026</strong>, needs only <strong>15 Crafting</strong>, long cleared. Speak to <strong>Talia at the Dog Shelter by Ice Mountain</strong> near the Edgeville Monastery. Bring a <strong>needle, thread, one fur and grain</strong> for the stuffed-dog phase, plus ordinary combat gear, a little food and empty space; the small outlaw encounter is not a midgame boss. Follow the shelter, Varrock and puppy trail as the journal directs. The reward opens the <strong>dog/puppy system</strong>; it is a Quest Cape requirement and a deliberately lighter change of pace, not a Jad power-up. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Ruff_Situation" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest guide</a> · <a href="https://www.jagex.com/news/old-school-runescape-goes-barking-mad-with-dog-themed-quest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jagex launch note</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-crab-quest" number="7" title="Quest break: complete Crab Quest">
        <p>Also released <strong>8 September 2026</strong>, this light Sailing quest needs <strong>40 Sailing and 30 Fishing</strong>, both already passed. Take your own boat to <strong>Dognose Island north-west of the Great Conch</strong> and drink the mysterious bottle on the beach. Leave roughly <strong>nine inventory spaces</strong> for the shells; the <strong>big fishing net</strong> used for the island's flotsam can be obtained during the quest. Explore, collect shells, help the crab assemble its instrument and finish the ceremony—no combat kit or supply grind. Claim <strong>10,000 Sailing and 3,000 Fishing XP</strong> and the <strong>shell collection</strong>. This completes another current Quest Cape requirement and breaks the training rhythm; its XP is not a Jad prerequisite. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crab_Quest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest guide</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i33-ranged-75" number="8" title="Resume cheap Ranged training to the normal actual-75 Jad target">
        <p>Use the same bone-bolt crab sessions or suitable Slayer tasks and inspect live XP as you go. <strong>Stop at actual 75 Ranged for the default first Fight Cave attempt.</strong> This is our preparation target, <strong>not a hard Fight Caves requirement</strong>: a confident player may try around 70, and if 75 feels uncomfortable after an attempt, train toward <strong>80</strong> before retrying. That is a bounded comfort adjustment, not failure and not a Bowfa/blowpipe dependency.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">TzHaar Fight Cave · mandatory Fire Cape</div><h2>Range Jad. Keep the prayer problem to two attack styles.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i33-fire-cape" number="9" title="Complete the ranged Fight Caves and obtain the Fire Cape">
        <p>Travel down the <strong>Karamja volcano entrance</strong> into <strong>Mor Ul Rek</strong>, then enter the <strong>TzHaar Fight Cave</strong> in its outer city. There are <strong>63 waves</strong>, ending with TzTok-Jad; this is a long endurance run, not 63 separate trips. Bring the deterministic <strong>adamant crossbow</strong> (or an RCB already owned), <strong>Ava's accumulator, green d'hide or better banked Ranged armour, Barrows gloves, a reasonable banked amulet and a shield/off-hand that does not ruin Ranged accuracy</strong>. Use <strong>Eagle Eye</strong>, real banked food and Prayer/restore potions; do not assume Rigour. For a first no-brew inventory, roughly <strong>14–17 four-dose Prayer/restore potions</strong> with the remaining slots mostly high-healing food is a starting layout, not a fixed rule—adjust from actual supply use on the first run. Pack plain adamant bolts for most waves and switch to <strong>diamond bolts (e)</strong> for Jad and other high-defence moments. Keep most ruby (e) stock for later high-HP quests. A Ranging potion is useful <em>only if already banked</em>; no Herblore detour. The holy wrench is optional because its slot competes with another restore or food. Blood spells can heal from a safespottable enemy <em>if</em> you already have spell access and runes, but the route never requires them. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/TzHaar_Fight_Cave/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current waves, spawns and strategy</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Waves: preserve supplies, control the mixed threats" label="Fight Cave primer">
          <p>Use rocks and corners to isolate melee enemies; a large monster can also body-block another enemy while you range around it. Prayer-draining Tz-Kihs deserve early attention, and the level-180 melee enemies can often be safespotted. Conserve Prayer on easy waves rather than leaving expensive prayers on while nothing can reach you. From <strong>wave 31</strong>, level-360 <strong>Ket-Zeks</strong> make <strong>Protect from Magic</strong> effectively central whenever one is free to attack. Later ranger-plus-mage combinations are the real resource pressure: block the mage, use terrain/body-blocking, and kill or isolate the ranger that threatens through your current prayer. Eat or restore during controlled gaps instead of waiting for a crisis. Do not try to memorize all 63 compositions; use the linked current wave/spawn guide.</p>
          <p><strong>Wave 62</strong> has two Ket-Zeks. Identify the <strong>orange/off-colour</strong> one: Jad will spawn at its location next wave. Before killing the last Ket-Zek, heal, restore Prayer, switch to the Jad bolts, locate a safe standing position and put the prayer tab in view. Start Jad with <strong>Protect from Missiles</strong> while watching his first tell; his Magic tell has an audible cue but the Ranged hit sound arrives too late to be a warning.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <ExpandableNote title="Jad and healers: one action between prayer checks" label="Ranged-only Jad plan">
          <p><strong>Stay outside Jad's melee range throughout.</strong> The mandatory plan is <strong>Ranged Jad</strong>, not a melee fallback. At range his core read is only <strong>two protection prayers</strong>: he <strong>slams his front feet down and cracks the ground → Protect from Missiles</strong>; he <strong>rears up with front feet dangling, growls/inhales, then breathes fire → Protect from Magic</strong>. Use the animation before the projectile; the Ranged sound after impact cannot save you. Watch <strong>Jad</strong>, not the inventory.</p>
          <p><strong>One action between prayer checks:</strong> identify an attack, switch/confirm the correct prayer, do <em>one</em> secondary action—tag one healer, drink one potion dose, eat one food or reposition once—then return your eyes to Jad for the next attack. Prayer switching is priority one. Do not chain several healer tags and potion doses while Jad is animating.</p>
          <p>At <strong>150 HP (60% remaining)</strong>, four Yt-HurKot healers appear. Tag them <strong>one at a time</strong> between Jad attacks and draw them far enough away that they stop healing him; keep checking every Jad animation. If a crossbow click might path you dangerously close to Jad, switch the crossbow to <strong>Longrange</strong> while tagging, then keep Jad outside melee reach. Healers are priority two. Do not panic or try to solve four tasks in one tick; if their damage becomes a problem, reposition or deal with them in controlled prayer cycles.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Death/retry rules:</strong> the Fight Caves is safe for ordinary accounts and <strong>solo Hardcore Ironmen</strong>, but <strong>not safe for Hardcore Group Ironman lives</strong>. The <a href="https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/summer-sweep-up---agility--chambers-of-xeric-changes?oldschool=1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">12 August 2026 update</a> removed the old re-entry cooldown, so a failed attempt can restart immediately. First attempts are information: note which mixed waves drained Prayer, where food vanished, whether healer tagging caused panic, and whether Jad's tells were read consistently. Adjust that specific issue, supplies or the bounded 75→80 comfort range before another run—<strong>not</strong> a mandatory rare-weapon farm. Finish the 63rd wave and claim the <strong>Fire Cape</strong>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.3 complete · guaranteed default-route exit</div>
        <h3>The Fire Cape is now part of the mandatory combat handoff.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quests complete:</strong> Troll Romance, The Curse of Arrav, A Ruff Situation and Crab Quest.</li>
          <li><strong>Measured combat:</strong> actual 75+ Ranged on the normal route; the earlier 62 was Arrav's quest gate, never the Jad target.</li>
          <li><strong>Equipment and stock:</strong> Fire Cape obtained, a deterministic adamant-crossbow floor (or already-owned RCB), and remaining plain/enchanted bolts carried forward. Check live bank quantities before later quest bosses.</li>
          <li><strong>Not guaranteed:</strong> RCB, blowpipe, Eclipse/Moon gear, Bowfa/crystal, black mask/Slayer helmet, Ava's assembler or Rigour. Optional drops never become required progress.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
